## 5. The editor in the block style (12.2, 12.3)

### The rule: chunky frame, calm rows

What floats over the view (a bar, a panel, a modal, a toast) is a **frame**: `--surface`, a `2px` ink edge, a hard shadow (`--shadow-md`: `0 4px 0 var(--edge)`), a radius of 12–14px, no blur, no translucency. What's inside a frame is a **row**: no edge or shadow of its own, separated by `1px var(--divider)` lines, hover and selection as a `--field` or `--accent-fill` background. Sizes are scaled to the editor's 13px base (the Control Panel's are for 16px): edges `2px` (not 2.5), shadows 4px for frames and 3px for buttons.

### Surface by surface

| Surface | Today | In the block style |
|---|---|---|
| tool-bar, contextual bar | dark glass, blurred | frames; tool buttons are small blocks (`--shadow-sm`, press down on click), the active tool a `--primary` block; the shortcut letter in `--mono`, `--ink-soft` |
| kind toggle (room, volume, hole) | segmented, dark | the Control Panel's segmented tabs: a `--field` track, the active one a raised `--surface` block |
| color swatches | round swatches | the palette's own colors (the view's, not the theme's), each with an ink edge; the active one lifted with a shadow |
| view bar (top right) | dark pills | a frame; toggles as blocks, an off toggle flat and `--ink-soft`; the theme toggle joins it |
| project bar, library toggle | dark pills | the project bar a frame at the wordmark's height, the library toggle a block button (`--accent-fill` when open) |
| outliner, Entities, Shots, Library panels | dark panels | frames; headers in `--display`; rows calm (selection `--accent-fill`, drop targets `--accent` lines); search fields as `--field` wells |
| inspector | dark floating panel | a frame; section labels in `--display`, `--ink-soft`; fields as `--field` wells with a `1.5px` edge that turns `--accent` on focus; steppers and choice buttons small blocks; numbers in `--mono` |
| modals (project picker, confirmations) | dark modal | a large frame (`--shadow-md` doubled) on a backdrop of `--paper` at 70% with its grid; primary buttons `--primary` blocks, danger `--danger-fill` |
| status bar (info-label) | dark strip | a `--surface` strip with an ink top edge; numbers `--mono`; the connection dot the Control Panel's pulsing `--ok` dot (`--danger` offline) |
| draft label, marquee | dark label, blue box | a small `--surface` tag with an ink edge; the marquee in `--accent` |
| error panel, crashed screen | dark | frames with a `--danger` edge; the crashed screen on `--paper` |
| compass rose | dark rim | a `--surface` rim with an ink edge; the needle keeps red for north |
| Walk HUD, pause menu | dark overlays | the pause menu a frame on the paper backdrop; the HUD's status and flash as small tags (the crosshair stays white with a dark outline, for any scene) |
| tooltips (`title`) | the browser's | unchanged |

Focus rings are the Control Panel's: `3px solid var(--accent)`, offset 2–3px, on `:focus-visible` only. `prefers-reduced-motion` turns off the wordmark's rise, the dot's pulse and the buttons' press transitions.

### The theme toggle (12.2)

One button at the end of the view bar (lucide's `SunMoon`, `Sun` or `Moon`) cycles **System → Light → Dark**, with its state in the tooltip (`Theme: System (dark now). Click for light`). `main.tsx` applies the stored choice to `<html data-theme>` before React renders, so there's no flash; System removes the attribute. It's per browser, in localStorage like the Library's and the stats readout's open state (`src/web/theme.ts`).

### The view's overlays (12.5)

What the editor draws over the level in the 3D view is one blue family today (the selection's tint and edges, a box's draft, the Pen, point handles, a selected note's outline), plus a red for a crossing outline and an orange for array handles. They move together to `src/ui/viewColors.ts`: `VIEW_ACCENT` (`--sky-d`), `VIEW_DANGER` (`--coral-d`), `VIEW_HANDLE` (`--peach-d`). Since the view stays light in both themes, these are the **light** theme's values in both, as constants (no need to read CSS at runtime), so they're always legible on the canvas. Captures never draw them. `ITEM_COLOR` (an array item's dot) is the palette's yellow and stays, as do the hover yellow and the axis colors.

### Where the editor's CSS goes

`src/web/styles.css` keeps its structure and comments; each rule's colors and fonts are replaced with tokens, and the frames, block buttons and wells are styled in the existing selectors (no new class names in the TSX, so no component changes). No prettier: format by hand, matching the file's current density.

